WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.620
If you haven't seen Avengers: Infinity War
yet, click away from this screen fast because

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.740
spoilers are coming … Still here?

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.100
"Woo!

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:08.860
Let's go!"

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.660
If Infinity War proved nothing else, it's
that directors Joe and Anthony Russo aren't

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.080
afraid to orchestrate some devastating consequences
for our favorite superheroes.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.000
Even Thanos' before the heartbreaking purge,
several major mainstays of the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.880
Universe met their makers, including Heimdall,
Loki, Gamora, and Vision.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.860
It may seem inevitable that the good guys
will ultimately win in Avengers 4, and maybe

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.620
even revive many of those lost in Infinity
War.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.460
But it's also just as likely that even more
heroes will fall to the Mad Titan before it's

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.440
all said and done.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.100
We can't definitively predict who will or
won't make it out alive next time, of course.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.540
But thanks to contract commitments of the
cast, the characters' comic origins, and other

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:54.640
details, we do have some educated guesses
about which characters might find themselves

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.640
on the chopping block in Avengers 4.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.240
The First Avenger

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.400
One of the most memorable moments of the comic
Infinity Gauntlet -- which inspired much of

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.620
the Infinity War -- happens when Captain America
marches on Thanos.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.540
In spite of being one of the less powerful
heroes facing him, Cap doesn't betray an ounce

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.040
of fear.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:18.300
In part, his attack is a ploy: Cap's distracting
Thanos so that Silver Surfer can try to snatch

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.960
the Infinity Gauntlet away from him.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:25.240
But even after that effort fails, Cap doesn't
back down, giving Thanos a crack across the

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.940
jaw before falling to the Mad Titan's might.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.780
We already saw something of a tribute to this
moment at the end of Infinity War, but there's

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.220
no way we've seen the last of Cap's hopeless
heroics.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.380
After all, Avengers 4 marks the end of Chris
Evans' contract with the studio, and the actor

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.200
has indicated he's ready to give up the role.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.300
"I don't know what's next but yeah, at this
point, by 2019 that's it."

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:53.280
If this does end up being his last MCU movie,
the filmmakers aren't likely to give Captain

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.160
America a quiet retirement ceremony.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.280
He already decided he'd rather be a hero than
settle down in Avengers: Age of Ultron, so

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:04.789
having him sit this one out while others take
the brunt of Thanos' punishment just isn't

00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:05.360
his style.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:10.360
If Captain America isn't going to be an Avenger
anymore, a heroic downfall seems like the

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.340
only way to end it.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.120
The lost daughter

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:17.340
Nebula is one of the most tragically flawed
characters of the MCU.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.680
She was a villain in the first Guardians of
the Galaxy film and a reluctant hero in the

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.180
second.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.800
The cruelty she experiences at the hands of
her father Thanos has left her blinded by

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.720
her thirst for vengeance against him.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.720
Thanks to her unbridled bloodlust, she tends
to make a lot of bad decisions.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.880
Her refusal to stay with her sister and the
Guardians at the end of Volume 2, for example,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.360
ultimately led to her capture by Thanos and
the torture session that inspired Gamora to

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.760
give up the goods on the Soul Stone's whereabouts
in Infinity War.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:51.080
Without her sister around to anchor her, she's
bound to make even more mistakes, and this

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.860
time, it may cost her her life.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.920
Even if her character's arc follows the comics
and sees her seize control of the Gauntlet,

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.280
that's not exactly good news for Nebula either.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.620
Expect her to finally fall at the hands of
her adopted father.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.880
The challenger to the throne

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:12.160
Comics fans may have been a bit surprised
by the courage and nobility displayed by M'Baku

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.140
in Black Panther and Infinity War.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.380
He's primarily known as the villain Man-Ape
in the comics, so M'Baku's on-screen challenge

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.000
to T'Challa's throne was to be expected.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:26.340
His last minute support of the King, however,
was a much less obvious route.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:34.980
"One more word, and I will feed you to my
children … I'm kidding we are vegetarians."

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:40.880
But the M'Baku of both the page and the screen
cares for his people, the Jabari, before all

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:41.380
else.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:46.260
With T'Challa being one of the victims of
Thanos' purge, M'Baku finds himself in an

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.400
unusual position.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:52.760
Wakanda is defeated, so he could use T'Challa's
absence as chance to seize the throne, even

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.380
though his days would probably be numbered.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:04:00.360
Either T'Challa would take him out upon his
inevitable return, or Okoye or Shuri would

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.260
do the job for him.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.980
M'Baku could also join the other heroes, and
even then, his number would likely come up

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:10.140
anyway; the chances of a M'Baku solo film
franchise are pretty thin.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:15.140
The named cast of Black Panther involved in
Infinity War is due to lose some of its numbers.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:17.320
The Last Guardian

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:23.560
Of all the survivors of Infinity War, Rocket
Raccoon will likely enter Avengers 4 as the

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.360
most distraught.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:29.800
Not only did he witness Groot's tear-jerking
final moments, but if and when the survivors

00:04:29.819 --> 00:04:34.139
from Titan get in touch with the Avengers
on Earth, he'll learn every friend he had

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.780
left in the universe is gone.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:41.860
Even surrounded by a ship full of compatriots,
Rocket is impulsive, depressed, quick to anger,

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.340
and bloodthirsty once he gets a gun in his
hands.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:50.139
In Guardians of the Galaxy, right after Ronan's
ship crashes on Xandar, Rocket hopelessly

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.920
charges the villain because of how worked
up he is over the original Groot's death.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.780
Now that he has nothing to lose, it's more
likely than ever that he'll do something stupid.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:03.040
If he gets Thanos in his crosshairs, he's
not going to care about the consequences.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.020
Even if it's fruitless from the start, we
can probably count on the little guy to run

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.600
headlong into harm's way to get revenge for
Groot 2.0.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:11.980
Rhodey

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.759
War Machine stands a fair chance of kicking
the bucket in Avengers 4 as well, for one

00:05:16.759 --> 00:05:21.559
good reason: of all the heroes to survive
Infinity War, he's the one that's already

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:25.000
deceased in the comics -- and at the hand
of Thanos, no less.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.669
He's also not exactly a Marvel A-lister, so
there's a question of what to do with Rhodey

00:05:29.669 --> 00:05:31.040
if he were to survive the story.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:35.800
In the comics, he replaced Stark as Iron Man
before taking up the role of War Machine,

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:41.120
but for now, Robert Downey Jr. has left such
a mark on the role that the idea of a non-Downey

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.900
Iron Man is all but impossible.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:45.060
"I hope they remember you."

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.540
The god of thunder

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:51.440
Not only is Chris Hemsworth's contract coming
to an end with Avengers 4, but the events

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:55.710
of Thor: Ragnarok and Infinity War might make
you wonder whether the character would even

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:56.300
want to survive.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.819
While Thor: Ragnarok ended on a hopeful note,
with a few dozen Asgardian survivors bound

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:06.339
for Earth to start life anew, Infinity War
opened with the slaughter of most of the people

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.040
Thor worked so hard to save.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:13.639
Most of those refugees have perished, Heimdall
and the Warriors Three are gone, and every

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.860
bit of Thor's family — blood-related or
otherwise — is history as well.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.220
And since Asgard is destroyed, Thor is now
a failed king.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:26.980
Even his fancy new weapon proved to be unable
to serve its purpose of taking out Thanos.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:31.580
With so much wreckage behind him already,
it's difficult to imagine anything beyond

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.880
a glorious demise would satisfy his warrior's
spirit at this point.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:36.800
The princess

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:41.680
Considering how popular Shuri has become since
the release of Black Panther, it's likely

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.600
comic book fans worried for her throughout
Infinity War.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.699
Marvel readers know that T'Challa's sister
held the mantle of Black Panther in the comics

00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:53.759
for some time, and eventually sacrificed her
life fighting Thanos' Cabal so that her brother

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:54.440
could escape.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:59.720
Popular though she is, if Shuri were to die
in Avengers 4, it could lead to an interesting

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:01.460
opportunity for Black Panther 2.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:06.919
When Ta-Nehisi Coates helped re-launch the
Black Panther comic series in 2016, he ended

00:07:06.919 --> 00:07:10.960
the first issue by revealing that T'Challa
was struggling with how to bring Shuri back

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:11.780
from the beyond.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:16.759
Eventually, Shuri did return — and with
powers connected to the ancestral origins

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:17.440
of Wakanda.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:22.979
If Shuri were to fall in Avengers 4 and return
in a fashion similar to her comic book resurrection,

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:28.040
it would give director Ryan Coogler a chance
to explore the more mystic side of Wakanda's

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:28.540
roots.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:29.940
The Monster

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:35.159
How else could Bruce Banner's story possibly
end but to see the big green giant disappear

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:35.660
forever?

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:40.160
It's not just that Mark Ruffalo's contract
is up with Avengers 4, or that the film is

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:44.980
expected to round-out his supposed trilogy
of Hulk stories that started with Thor: Ragnarok.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.640
There also just aren't many imaginable futures
left for the character.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:54.840
As we saw in Infinity War, Hulk was hesitant
to come out and do the Avengers' bidding against

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:55.340
Thanos.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:00.479
Perhaps it's because Thanos gave him a brutal
beating like no other, but perhaps it also

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:04.879
has something to do with the fact that Banner
feels like he disappears altogether whenever

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.520
he's transformed into the Other Guy.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.960
In either case, the Hulk is not well-liked
on Earth, thanks to his violently reckless

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.100
behavior in Age of Ultron.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:17.020
The only chance that he might change anyone's
mind about him is if he goes out a hero and

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.960
saves more lives than he's cost the world
in the past.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.140
Thanks for watching!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.800
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:23.809 --> 00:08:26.069
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

